# The package description for tools/package.py (NBTFoundry/manager): one argument
# per line. `make doom-package` and the release workflow both use it; they add the
# version, sequence, key, output and executable. Bridge 1.7: the payload is a
# guest (GPL code runs only as a guest), run by NBT Manager's nbt-runner
# (runner).
--app
doom
--compat
nbt_6.5_armv7
--bridge
1.7
--bridge-uses
show,controller,runner
--bridge-optional
status,live-settings,gamepad
--setting
turn_sens|Turn Sensitivity|medium|low,medium,high
--setting
invert_turn|Invert Turn|off|off,on
--setting
brightness|Brightness|2|0,1,2,3,4
--setting
always_run|Always Run|on|off,on
--setting
sound|Sound|on|off,on
--setting
show_fps|Show FPS|off|off,on
--setting
debug_log|Debug log|off|off,on
# What the phone app shows before an install (NBT Manager's PROTOCOL.md,
# "Package information"): the PrBoom+ version the pin builds
# (tools/package_version.py: `make package-args`; `make test` checks it), the
# project, the licence and the notices.
--property
PrBoom+|2.6.66
--property
Project|PrBoom+ (https://github.com/coelckers/prboom-plus)
--property
Licence|GPL-2.0-or-later
--text
Doom by PrBoom+, with NBTFoundry's changes for NBT Manager.
--text=
--text
Includes the Doom shareware episode (doom1.wad): id Software's game data, not under the GPL.
--text=
--text
Source, licences and notices: https://github.com/NBTFoundry/nf-doom
